{
  "_comment": [
    "One registry entity per seeded device. They are no longer what keeps the devices alive —",
    "the config entry in core.config_entries is (see that file) — but they are what makes the",
    "pair look like a real integration's: an entity under the device, owned by the same entry.",
    "",
    "History: until HA 2026.7 these rows were the devices' only anchor against",
    "helpers/device_registry.async_cleanup, which deletes a device referenced by neither a live",
    "config entry nor an entity. From 2026.8 that anchor is not enough — the device registry's",
    "v3 migration drops an entry-less device before any cleanup runs.",
    "",
    "Their platform is `acme`, the seeded entry's domain, deliberately not the fixture's custom",
    "component, so they cannot be mistaken for entities `cc show` should attribute.",
    "",
    "Side effect, recorded rather than discovered later: `acme` is not installed, so HA publishes",
    "each of these as a RESTORED ghost — state `unavailable`, attribute `restored: true`. That",
    "is a real shape a real instance has (the reference instance carries 37 of them) and the rig",
    "had none.",
    "",
    "Key set and minor_version taken from the loader in the image",
    "(helpers/entity_registry.py, _async_load), not guessed: HA indexes these keys directly and",
    "KeyErrors on a missing one."
  ],
